body.statement:
Open-ended Question 1 (rational replacement of a feasible separator). For every finite syntactically certified input with \(\mathcal M_{\mathcal I}^{\circ}
eq\varnothing\), every pair \(D,D'\in\mathfrak D\), and every outcome cell \(y\) for which \(\mathcal M_{\mathcal I}^{\circ}\cap\{p:F_{D,D',y}(p)
eq0\}
eq\varnothing\), must there also exist a strictly positive rational exact-oracle table \(p^\dagger\in\mathcal M_{\mathcal I}^{\circ}\cap\mathbb Q^{\Omega}\) with \(F_{D,D',y}(p^\dagger)
eq0\); and, when such a rational replacement exists, can its height be bounded effectively from the finite input?
